---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { providers } from "../lib/data";
---

<Base title="How we checked" description="Sources, confidence tags, dates, and the limits of this research.">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="kicker">Method</p>
    <h1>How we checked</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every claim on this site comes from a provider's own documentation, pricing page, or a named
      third party. Each one carries a confidence tag, a quote and a link. Nothing is inferred into a
      fact, and nothing unpublished is estimated.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="measure">
    <h2>What was done</h2>
    <p>
      For each provider, a researcher read the documentation, the pricing page, the FAQ, the terms
      and, where it existed, the machine-readable OpenAPI or documentation bundle. Each profile
      records the exact quote, its URL, and a tag. The profiles are kept in the repository under
      <span class="mono">experiments/sandbox-comparison/research/</span>.
    </p>
    <p>
      No account was created, no sandbox was started, and nothing was billed. That means every
      statement about behaviour is a documentation claim, not a measurement. Where a provider's
      documentation contradicts itself, both statements are shown and the row is marked as a
      contradiction.
    </p>

    <h2>Confidence tags</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Tag</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.confidenceTags.map((tag) => (
            <tr>
              <td><span class="confidence">{tag.tag}</span></td>
              <td>{tag.meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Dates</h2>
    <p>
      All seven profiles were checked on {site.checkedOn}. Prices changed during October 2026 at
      several providers — boxd cut its rates by about 20% between 9 and 28 October, and Boat moved
      from credit packs to a dollar wallet — so treat any number here as a dated observation, not a
      standing fact. Boat's documentation is served through a cache that can return an older revision,
      so its figures were re-fetched with cache-busting URLs and come from the live pages, not the
      cached copies.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits worth stating plainly</h2>
    <ul>
      {site.limits.map((limit) => <li>{limit}</li>)}
    </ul>

    <h2>About battleships.dev</h2>
    <p>
      battleships.dev is a comparison dataset built by the Boat (boat.dev) team. We used it as a
      cross-check and never as a primary source. It disagreed with live provider pages often enough
      that its numbers are not repeated here as fact: it described InstaBox's pricing and sizes as
      they were before 20 October, boxd's rates as they were on 14 October, and Runtime's idle
      default as it was before 18 October. Its own Boat record is dated 30 September and disagrees
      with Boat's current docs on disk sizes and snapshot retention.
    </p>
    <p>
      That does not make it useless. It is a fast way to find out which questions to ask. It is a bad
      way to settle a price.
    </p>

    <h2>Open questions we could not settle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Why Sandboxer's sizes, hourly rates and plan tiers match Boat's exactly while its disk sizes, regions, stopped-disk retention and legal entity differ. No public source explains the relationship.</li>
      <li>Whether Agent 37's Cloud dashboard can create a sandbox by clicking. No documented path exists, but the absence may be a documentation gap.</li>
      <li>Whether InstaBox's free plan requires a card. The pricing page says no; the API has a state that says yes.</li>
      <li>What a stored snapshot costs at Lizard, and what backup storage costs at boxd. Neither is published.</li>
      <li>Whether egress is free at Agent 37, boxd and Boat. None publishes a rate or a cap.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Per-provider sources</h2>
    <ul>
      {providers.map((provider) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/providers/${provider.id}/`}>{provider.name}</a> — checked {provider.checkedOn},{" "}
          {provider.caveats.length} recorded caveats
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
